 Experimental native-stereo 6DOF OpenVR mod for the 32-bit Steam release of
 Bayonetta (executable timestamp `0x591AD330`).
 
+## Corrected floor calibration (build 20261011.56)
+
+Hold **L3+R3 for one second** on a player-one gamepad or both VR thumbsticks.
+Keep Bayonetta standing on ordinary flat ground and wear the headset at your
+normal playing height. F8 also calibrates. **Shift+F8 clears calibration** and
+restores the original camera/recenter behavior immediately. Startup keeps the
+original camera until calibration succeeds. `FloorCalibration=0` disables the
+feature; gamepad calibration is independent of Touch input emulation.
+
+Calibration uses the VR runtime's configured standing-space floor and the
+player's feet position. It levels game-camera pitch/roll and adjusts eye height
+without changing world scale. Subsequent game-camera vertical movement remains,
+so different terrain or camera elevation can need recalibration. The feet
+reference is not a terrain raycast: calibrate while grounded, not during a jump.
+Missing or invalid reference data preserves an existing calibration; before the
+first successful calibration it performs the original recenter instead.
+
+The .55 failure was a handedness error: the game uses a right-handed look-at and
+projection, and recovering its view through the mod's left-handed projection
+produces a reflected basis. Replacing that basis with a positive-determinant
+one reflected the whole scene, reversing horizontal directions and triangle
+winding. .56 preserves the basis sign and refuses any correction that would
+reflect, scale or otherwise violate an orthogonal camera transform.
+
+Regression tests execute the original Steam camera routines (`C5A160` and
+`C5A580`), resolving the game's actual D3DX and CRT imports. The GPU test
+reproduces .55's black/reversed image in all 18 stereo cases with face culling
+enabled, then verifies .56 against a separately constructed native-engine
+camera over 294,912 pixels. Another 3,150 cases cover both basis signs, head
+and camera tilt, height, scale, stereo, the physical floor plane and invalid
+input. Successful calibration logs both camera and correction determinants.
+This regression reproduces the reported failure; final comfort/floor alignment
+still needs a headset check. The archived .55 evidence remains in
+`.diagnostics/failed55-20261011-223721`.
+
+Release/Win32, the full regression suite and companion transport tests pass.
+Both .56 components are installed with existing settings preserved and
+`FloorCalibration=1`. Previous .54 files are saved under
+`.diagnostics/before56-20261011-224948`.
+Installed DLL SHA256:
+`C1787F59D8EE0FD5170CBA7E29CE4D6BABA2E34C2ED22779006ACF70212A82A1`.
+Installed companion SHA256:
+`3728BC1DB48C01FB9A554AE5737731976556EC295B6C711177320EBF7707EA6B`.
+
